  "basis": "The dashboard displays a bar chart titled 'Browser Usage Share by Product'. There is a conflict between the bar heights (Safari is visually the tallest) and the printed data labels (Chrome is labeled 73%, Safari 12%). The printed data labels are the explicit quantitative values provided for the 'Usage Share' metric. Comparing the printed labels for the selectable options, Chrome (73%) has a significantly higher share than Safari (12%) and Firefox (6%). Therefore, Chrome is the primary compatibility target based on the explicit data values.",
  "option_label": "Set Chrome as the primary compatibility target"
}
